"Drama 3" -- Fish Audio's guide to directing its Drama 3 text-to-speech
model -- is by Fish Audio, published in its documentation
(https://docs.fish.audio/features/text-to-speech/drama-3, source
https://github.com/fishaudio/docs, commit
70296af6bcb0fbf3f20cb1c65a0143c565f7e859) under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International license (LICENSE, beside this file, as
published in that repository).

Valtz includes the guide unmodified:

  drama-3.mdx

and uses it, with Valtz's own instructions, in its prompt enhancer when
the target model is Drama 3. Valtz reads it as plain text, which changes
what the model is handed: the page's front matter, imports and closing
component are left out, as are its "What's new", "Voice cast" and "How to
use" sections and its shell example (they are about Fish Audio's web
service); each audio example is given as the line it speaks, and each
warning as a note. The file here is the page as published.

Drama 3's weights are Fish Audio's too, under the Fish Audio Community
License; Valtz does not ship them (Settings > Capabilities downloads
them from Hugging Face, with that license, as published).
